WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
kanashige ni saku hana ni kimi no omokage wo mita

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
I saw your image in the flower that is blossoming sorrowfully

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
daisuki na ame nanoni naze ka kyou wa tsumetakute

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
I love rain, yet it felt frosty today

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
kisetsu wa meguri mori wa somerare kaze wa kanadete omoi afurete

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
The season changed, the forest was colored, the wind played a tune, memories overflowed

00:37.600 --> 00:46.786
tsuki no kakera wo atsumete yume wo kazari nemuru

00:37.600 --> 00:46.787
Gather the pieces of the moon, decorate the dream and sleep

00:47.020 --> 00:56.153
toki no suna chiribametemo ano koro e kaeranai

00:47.020 --> 00:56.154
Even if I sprinkle the sand of time, I cannot return to the past

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
ikiru imi sageshiteiru dare mo mina tabibito

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
Those searching for the meaning of life are all travellers

01:05.769 --> 01:14.817
haruka naru tabiji tadori boku wa ima arukidasu

01:05.776 --> 01:14.817
I set my course on this endless journey

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
ibara no michi no mukou e...

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
for the place beyond the thorny path...

01:25.825 --> 01:30.745
The artist of life who produces miracles
with his godlike scalpel skills.

01:31.664 --> 01:33.999
The surgeon whom the era has yearned for.

01:34.875 --> 01:35.918
Black Jack.

01:49.768 --> 01:50.907
Largo!

01:51.755 --> 01:53.016
Largo!

01:54.462 --> 01:57.075
Largo, time for dinner!

01:57.800 --> 01:59.008
Where did she go?

02:01.178 --> 02:03.596
Largo!

02:04.860 --> 02:07.194
Sheesh, Largo, where have you been?

02:07.195 --> 02:08.571
It's time for dinner.

02:11.074 --> 02:12.074
What's this?

02:14.536 --> 02:16.662
Ohmigewdness!

02:17.748 --> 02:18.706
Doc!

02:18.916 --> 02:19.624
What?

02:19.625 --> 02:20.583
What's the matter, Pinoco?

02:20.584 --> 02:22.126
This, this, this!

02:22.127 --> 02:23.383
Look at this!

02:23.629 --> 02:24.651
Is this real?

02:28.896 --> 02:32.056
Originally by Tezuka Osamu "A Killer Whale's Songs”

02:28.896 --> 02:32.056
The Gift from A Killer Whale

02:32.930 --> 02:34.430
This way.

02:34.681 --> 02:37.934
Largo walked out from here with that in her mouth.

02:38.602 --> 02:40.717
There's only rocks and ocean beyond this,

02:41.021 --> 02:44.916
but maybe she found some treasure.

02:45.233 --> 02:46.651
She may have.

02:49.529 --> 02:50.916
Where are you going?

02:51.323 --> 02:52.823
Where the treasure is.

02:52.824 --> 02:55.451
Wait! I'll come too!

02:56.787 --> 02:59.622
Largo, Doc, wait.

03:01.208 --> 03:03.167
Oh, a cave.

03:03.168 --> 03:05.019
It's dark!

03:05.287 --> 03:06.128
Be careful.

03:08.882 --> 03:11.300
It's creepy.

03:18.475 --> 03:20.685
We're finally out.

03:27.192 --> 03:29.235
It's a pretty place!

03:29.653 --> 03:32.780
Why haven't you shown me this before?

03:36.118 --> 03:38.953
Hey, Largo, you'll catch a cold.

03:38.954 --> 03:40.496
Come back.

03:49.715 --> 03:50.840
Another pearl!

03:51.592 --> 03:53.009
There should be a lot more.

03:53.844 --> 03:54.677
Really?

04:02.352 --> 04:03.894
No way!

04:04.771 --> 04:06.997
So many!

04:08.150 --> 04:09.675
Are they all pearls?

04:09.766 --> 04:10.901
Can I take them?

04:10.902 --> 04:11.326
Yeah.

04:24.333 --> 04:26.287
You got what you deserved for being greedy.

04:26.627 --> 04:28.586
I haven't taken anything yet.

04:28.587 --> 04:30.796
Largo is the one who took some.

04:32.049 --> 04:36.677
Hey, Doc, why are there so many pearls here?

04:37.179 --> 04:39.862
They are all my friend's.

04:40.390 --> 04:41.349
Your friend?

04:41.350 --> 04:41.878
Yeah.

04:42.309 --> 04:44.352
It's been ten years since we parted.

04:46.980 --> 04:48.689
He came from the sea.

04:58.075 --> 05:02.627
Ten years ago, I built a clinic on this southern cape.

05:03.413 --> 05:08.376
But due to my scary appearance and
rumors of my outrageous fees,

05:08.377 --> 05:11.003
nobody came close to this clinic.

05:14.258 --> 05:16.467
I was truly lonely.

05:19.596 --> 05:22.265
No patients again today, huh?

05:28.188 --> 05:29.313
What's that noise?

05:34.987 --> 05:36.028
It's coming from below.

05:47.749 --> 05:48.541
That's...

05:55.841 --> 05:56.924
That's pretty bad.

05:57.551 --> 05:58.436
What happened?

05:58.844 --> 05:59.719
What got you?

06:05.392 --> 06:07.560
You're pretty weak.

06:08.145 --> 06:10.730
Hey, I'm not trying to harm you.

06:11.231 --> 06:15.192
Don't worry, I'm a doctor, albeit for humans.

06:16.820 --> 06:18.070
Is this from a bite?

06:19.197 --> 06:20.323
You're a mammal too.

06:20.407 --> 06:22.033
I should be able to apply first aid.

06:24.870 --> 06:27.717
You are my first patient in this town.

06:28.332 --> 06:29.787
This treatment is on me.

06:31.501 --> 06:33.381
That was our first encounter.

06:40.302 --> 06:42.345
Stay still for four to five days.

06:42.721 --> 06:44.994
Then you'll be able to swim again.

06:46.183 --> 06:49.936
From that day on, I couldn't forget about that killer whale.

06:51.438 --> 06:55.025
Two days later, I went out to this inlet.

06:59.655 --> 07:01.614
He must have gone back to the ocean.

07:12.709 --> 07:14.961
Hey! Don't be so reckless yet!

07:22.761 --> 07:26.911
I heard that wild animals recover
quickly, so I guess it's true.

07:29.268 --> 07:30.017
What's this?

07:32.562 --> 07:33.918
It's a pearl!

07:34.189 --> 07:35.147
You're gonna give it to me?

07:36.817 --> 07:37.670
I see.

07:37.943 --> 07:39.902
You have good etiquette.

07:40.445 --> 07:41.070
I'll take it.

07:41.071 --> 07:41.487
Thank you.

07:43.407 --> 07:47.034
To me, he looked happy.

07:48.912 --> 07:51.520
Our friendship began that day.

08:02.092 --> 08:03.259
Excuse me.

08:04.886 --> 08:07.224
Can you share some of those fish with me?

08:07.389 --> 08:09.090
Those are bad, so we're gonna throw them away.

08:09.516 --> 08:11.645
Go to the market to buy fish.

08:12.019 --> 08:14.812
Yes, but those are good enough.

08:15.147 --> 08:16.772
Are you gonna feed a cat or something?

08:16.773 --> 08:18.816
Yes, something like that.

08:19.818 --> 08:21.235
Here, take this.

08:22.112 --> 08:23.279
I don't need any money.

08:24.197 --> 08:24.947
Thanks.

08:26.742 --> 08:28.571
Dad, who's that?

08:28.827 --> 08:29.994
He doesn't look like a good guy.

08:30.621 --> 08:32.496
Get your work done before we chitchat!

08:32.497 --> 08:33.456
Yeah, yeah.

08:37.002 --> 08:37.501
There!

08:46.219 --> 08:49.337
Before long, it became my daily routine to see him.

08:50.307 --> 08:51.182
One of those days...

08:55.979 --> 08:57.063
Hey, what happened?!

08:57.522 --> 08:59.774
He became my patient again.

09:00.692 --> 09:02.818
Did you get hurt again?

09:02.819 --> 09:04.028
There are bruises too.

09:05.364 --> 09:06.629
Did you hit a rock?

09:06.907 --> 09:08.491
Or did you fight another whale?

09:09.409 --> 09:13.829
A ruffian like you should stay in the hospital for a while!

09:14.915 --> 09:16.666
Don't complain if it stings a little!

09:17.584 --> 09:21.921
Sheesh, maybe I should quit seeing
people, and just become a vet.

09:27.177 --> 09:28.592
Steer the boat right.

09:28.804 --> 09:29.999
Or else the fish will get away.

09:30.352 --> 09:31.849
Shut up! I'm doing it!

09:31.989 --> 09:34.998
Hell, like you know what's right.

09:41.108 --> 09:42.942
Hey, he's that guy from the other day...

09:43.986 --> 09:45.120
What's wrong, Dad?

09:45.404 --> 09:46.150
It's nothing.

09:46.446 --> 09:47.470
Look straight ahead.

09:49.533 --> 09:50.783
There, I'm done.

09:51.451 --> 09:54.641
Since this is a return visit, it'll cost you 200,000 yen.

10:00.586 --> 10:02.336
You were ready, huh?

10:02.838 --> 10:03.609
Fine, then.

10:06.383 --> 10:09.220
I gave him the name, Triton,

10:09.511 --> 10:10.720
and created a medical record for him.

10:11.722 --> 10:14.432
His medical file grew quickly.

10:16.310 --> 10:20.313
He was injured at least once every ten
days, and came back to this inlet.

10:21.231 --> 10:24.817
And he always brought something as payment.

10:25.569 --> 10:27.913
Most of the time, he brought pearls as payment,

10:28.196 --> 10:30.114
but sometimes he brought coral or old coins.

10:31.742 --> 10:36.120
Eventually, we built up a strange,
yet wonderful friendship.

10:43.921 --> 10:45.004
Thanks for everything.

10:45.297 --> 10:46.398
I don't mind.

10:46.632 --> 10:48.049
We'd be throwing them away otherwise.

10:48.467 --> 10:50.968
Anyway, you're here just about every morning.

10:51.470 --> 10:54.055
It must be a rather large cat.

10:54.556 --> 10:56.265
Well, yeah.

11:01.813 --> 11:04.398
Hey, can you come to the Union meeting?

11:04.399 --> 11:05.900
We need to talk about the killer whale hunt.

11:05.395 --> 11:06.812
I won't come.

11:07.194 --> 11:08.486
My son will go in my place.

11:08.904 --> 11:09.626
Dad...

11:09.821 --> 11:10.796
Oh, man...

11:11.448 --> 11:14.283
By the way, is that man your friend?

11:14.284 --> 11:15.052
No.

11:15.535 --> 11:18.996
He's a doctor who just opened
a clinic on the southern cape.

11:18.997 --> 11:19.732
A doctor?

11:20.040 --> 11:24.377
I guess he's highly skilled, but everyone
is too scared to go see him.

11:26.088 --> 11:27.171
A doctor, huh?

11:36.974 --> 11:38.754
Hey! Triton! Wait!

11:55.242 --> 11:56.242
Why, you...!

11:58.120 --> 12:00.204
I swam with Triton many times.

12:01.415 --> 12:03.993
One day, I met his friend.

12:04.668 --> 12:06.127
Hey, that's...

12:08.755 --> 12:11.132
Hey, do you wanna play too?

12:31.570 --> 12:33.195
Don't worry.

12:33.196 --> 12:34.652
I don't mind.

12:42.758 --> 12:45.260
Damn, the killer whale got us again!

12:45.678 --> 12:48.358
He breaks the net, and wreaks havoc on the fishing spot.

12:48.598 --> 12:49.606
Damn whale!

12:49.891 --> 12:52.559
On top of that he comes back
every time we chase him off!

12:52.935 --> 12:55.770
And there are people who have seen him with bandages.

12:55.771 --> 12:56.813
No way.

12:56.814 --> 12:58.719
A killer whale can't use bandages.

12:59.108 --> 13:00.317
My dad's too old-fashioned.

13:00.693 --> 13:04.571
He only talks about the old days,
and keeps the killer whale free.

13:12.622 --> 13:13.580
It's you.

13:14.040 --> 13:15.806
Sorry, but we don't have any today.

13:15.875 --> 13:17.417
We couldn't catch any fish.

13:17.418 --> 13:19.252
No, I wanted to ask you something.

13:19.712 --> 13:20.754
Oh yeah?

13:20.755 --> 13:23.256
I was just thinking that I wanted to talk with you too.

13:24.675 --> 13:27.844
Do you want to go out to the ocean?

13:30.681 --> 13:31.448
How's that?

13:31.849 --> 13:33.725
The ocean feels good too, doesn't it?

13:33.726 --> 13:34.260
Yes.

13:34.560 --> 13:36.588
So, how's that killer whale doing?

13:37.021 --> 13:37.854
How did you know?

13:38.356 --> 13:40.190
I happened to see you.

13:40.942 --> 13:45.390
We fishermen always coexisted with them.

13:46.072 --> 13:47.433
They catch fish.

13:47.698 --> 13:49.142
We catch fish, too.

13:49.534 --> 13:51.660
We recognized each other's lives.

13:52.161 --> 13:54.826
We could live side by side on the ocean.

13:55.623 --> 13:58.458
But now that's a thing of the past.

13:59.043 --> 14:00.487
This is a fair warning.

14:00.670 --> 14:02.504
Don't get involved with the killer whale anymore.

14:02.964 --> 14:05.298
A major killer whale hunt will start soon.

14:05.758 --> 14:09.017
But the killer whale has the right
to live freely in the ocean!

14:09.345 --> 14:10.262
That's right.

14:10.805 --> 14:13.473
But we have to make a living too!

14:15.768 --> 14:19.646
After all, humans and killer whales live in different worlds.

14:23.609 --> 14:26.444
Triton, so you've been ruining the fishing spots.

14:27.154 --> 14:29.990
All the injuries came from the fishermen, huh?

14:30.783 --> 14:33.155
Triton, you should go back to the ocean,

14:33.953 --> 14:35.842
and never come back here.

14:36.706 --> 14:38.415
Or else, you will be...

14:42.211 --> 14:43.727
Good bye, Triton.

14:44.046 --> 14:46.301
And we shall see each other
somewhere in the sea, someday.

14:51.095 --> 14:55.182
After that, I stayed away from the inlet for a few days.

14:58.477 --> 15:01.062
So, did Triton go back to the ocean?

15:02.023 --> 15:06.359
Back then, I believed that he went back to the ocean...

15:08.196 --> 15:09.791
Until that incident happened.

15:13.618 --> 15:14.360
Wait!

15:14.577 --> 15:16.077
Wait, damn whale!

15:17.997 --> 15:19.497
Where? Where did he go?!

15:19.498 --> 15:20.533
Slow down!

15:20.708 --> 15:22.042
The engine will burn out.

15:22.043 --> 15:23.919
Damn, I'll kill him today!

15:38.559 --> 15:39.893
Dad...

15:40.811 --> 15:41.937
Dad!

15:42.813 --> 15:44.606
Dad! Move, Dad!

15:45.149 --> 15:46.107
Dad!

15:47.818 --> 15:49.069
Dad!

15:59.121 --> 16:01.831
I was safe, since I clung to the boat,

16:01.832 --> 16:03.542
but the whale got Dad.

16:03.960 --> 16:04.668
That's absurd!

16:05.002 --> 16:07.420
A killer whale attacking a fishing boat?

16:07.463 --> 16:08.354
It's true!

16:08.589 --> 16:12.342
When our boats got there, there
was still a killer whale around!

16:12.343 --> 16:14.678
That one had a crescent on its back fin.

16:14.679 --> 16:15.720
What?!

16:15.721 --> 16:18.056
That damn whale must have been ready to eat him!

16:18.975 --> 16:22.769
If I'd known, I would've killed him sooner.

16:24.772 --> 16:26.291
How... How's Dad?

16:26.607 --> 16:28.400
He's in critical condition.

16:29.026 --> 16:32.529
We don't have any staff who can save him.

16:33.865 --> 16:34.865
No way...

16:35.408 --> 16:36.668
I will handle this case.

16:38.077 --> 16:41.246
I will save your dad, I promise.

16:46.936 --> 16:48.323
Operation in Progress

16:51.883 --> 16:54.323
Doctor, please.

16:57.388 --> 16:58.346
Inject fosmin.

16:58.347 --> 16:59.389
Blood transfusion too.

16:59.390 --> 17:00.891
Hurry with artificial heart-lung.

17:00.892 --> 17:01.423
Yes!

17:06.022 --> 17:07.814
Kill the man-eating whale!

17:08.357 --> 17:10.066
Don't miss him!

17:12.320 --> 17:12.944
Clamp.

17:12.945 --> 17:13.486
Here.

17:13.863 --> 17:14.696
Blood pressure?

17:14.697 --> 17:15.530
80.

17:15.531 --> 17:16.836
I can't read the low value.

17:17.158 --> 17:18.283
Inject fosmin.

17:18.284 --> 17:18.867
Yes!

17:31.881 --> 17:33.496
Operation complete.

17:46.896 --> 17:49.761
But I couldn't forget...

17:51.192 --> 17:52.526
About Triton.

18:07.124 --> 18:07.832
No.

18:08.584 --> 18:10.085
I can't treat you this time.

18:12.838 --> 18:14.551
Don't look at me like that!

18:15.049 --> 18:16.132
Give up and go back!

18:24.433 --> 18:27.352
<i>I told you not to come back.</i>

18:30.731 --> 18:36.057
Triton came back the next day, with
all the injuries and a new gift.

18:37.613 --> 18:40.156
Knowing that, I pretended that I didn't see him.

18:41.367 --> 18:45.453
Triton brought pearls and coral day
after day, getting weaker each time.

18:46.289 --> 18:47.080
Four,

18:47.540 --> 18:48.582
then five...

18:48.958 --> 18:52.252
Day after day, there were more gifts in the inlet.

18:53.546 --> 18:54.713
Please stop now.

18:55.172 --> 18:57.127
I don't want pearls or coral.

18:57.508 --> 18:58.479
I can't treat you!

18:58.885 --> 19:01.052
I just can't treat you anymore!

19:08.853 --> 19:10.520
Dad! Can you hear me?

19:10.521 --> 19:11.605
It's me, Dad!

19:12.398 --> 19:16.568
Don't talk so loud, idiot.

19:17.528 --> 19:21.198
We conquered that damn killer
whale while you were asleep.

19:21.782 --> 19:22.563
What?

19:22.783 --> 19:24.326
That crescent whale!

19:25.745 --> 19:27.787
The crescent whale?

19:28.831 --> 19:29.581
But...

19:29.957 --> 19:33.293
How could you do that?!

19:35.046 --> 19:40.569
Yes, there was a killer whale coming for me.

19:40.927 --> 19:46.431
Unable to move from the injury, I thought I was done for.

19:46.807 --> 19:47.641
Right then,

19:49.435 --> 19:55.190
another killer whale with a crescent on its fin
came, and chased away the other killer whale.

19:55.942 --> 20:01.081
On top of that, it carried me to the other people's boat.

20:01.948 --> 20:04.115
And did you kill him?

20:04.116 --> 20:04.908
No way...

20:05.451 --> 20:07.661
So the whale we chased away was...

20:09.288 --> 20:10.330
Doctor...?

20:16.212 --> 20:16.962
Triton!

20:20.883 --> 20:21.508
Triton!

20:23.511 --> 20:24.135
Triton!

20:26.931 --> 20:27.764
He's still alive!

20:29.016 --> 20:31.560
Triton, I won't let you die!

20:47.994 --> 20:51.288
Triton, this is not the place for you to live.

20:52.164 --> 20:55.025
This really is farewell.

21:10.683 --> 21:13.518
And nobody has seen Triton since.

21:20.818 --> 21:22.277
That's the end of the story.

21:24.197 --> 21:25.778
Don't tell anyone about this.

21:26.199 --> 21:26.980
Let's go back.

21:27.325 --> 21:31.536
Hey, Doc, you're not alone anymore, right?

21:33.456 --> 21:34.122
No.

21:36.709 --> 21:38.376
Largo, what's the...

21:43.758 --> 21:45.509
Doc, that's...

21:46.385 --> 21:47.427
Triton!

21:47.428 --> 21:49.596
It must be Triton!

21:51.807 --> 21:52.766
You're right.

21:54.060 --> 21:57.020
Triton!

21:57.313 --> 22:01.024
Take care!

22:07.080 --> 22:19.035
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

22:07.080 --> 22:19.035
daisukuyo anata to hitotsu ni nareru no nara

22:19.153 --> 22:24.152
I couldn't be happier...

22:19.153 --> 22:24.152
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

22:25.721 --> 22:31.190
I wanted to see you forever

22:25.721 --> 22:31.190
zutto aitakute mattetano

22:31.734 --> 22:37.192
I'm laying on the grill,

22:31.734 --> 22:37.192
ami no ue ni yasashiku nekasete

22:37.796 --> 22:40.281
being heated up by you,

22:37.796 --> 22:40.281
anata ni hoterasarete

22:40.490 --> 22:48.267
so much that I change color

22:40.490 --> 22:48.267
atashi wa iro ga kawarukurai

22:48.352 --> 23:00.121
I dress up with sparkly grains of decorations

22:48.352 --> 23:00.121
kirakira hikaru tsubu no kazari de oshare

23:00.329 --> 23:12.060
I love you darling. Please love me more and more...

23:00.329 --> 23:12.060
daisukiyo motto motto atashi wo aishite

23:12.300 --> 23:23.651
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

23:12.300 --> 23:23.651
daisukiyo anata to hitotsu no nareru no nara

23:23.837 --> 23:28.758
I couldn't be happier

23:23.837 --> 23:28.758
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

23:28.986 --> 23:33.920
How does it taste?

23:28.986 --> 23:33.919
oaji wa ikaga?

23:45.089 --> 24:15.032
Give Back My Brother!

23:45.209 --> 23:46.749
Big Mask!

23:47.721 --> 23:49.507
So cute!

23:49.888 --> 23:51.975
Gorass is your brother, right?

23:52.148 --> 23:55.099
So your brother's a bad guy.

23:55.435 --> 23:56.175
No, he's not!

23:57.015 --> 23:58.015
My legs...

23:58.201 --> 23:59.648
They're really swollen.

24:00.001 --> 24:03.141
Why are you the humanoid Gorass?

24:03.378 --> 24:05.598
I may cut him.

24:07.152 --> 24:10.092
This will sting you a bit.

